Let me check the current config for the subdomain.

> run: cat /etc/nginx/sites-available/newapp.conf

```
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name newapp.example.com;
    root /var/www/newapp;
}
```

It only serves port 80 with no redirect. I'll add an HTTPS server block and redirect HTTP:

> run: cat > /tmp/newapp.conf << 'NGINX'
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name newapp.example.com;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name newapp.example.com;
    root /var/www/newapp;
    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/newapp.example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/newapp.example.com/privkey.pem;
}
NGINX

> run: cp /tmp/newapp.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/newapp.conf && nginx -t && systemctl reload nginx

```
nnginx: the configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf syntax is ok
nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test is successful
```

Config updated and reloaded. HTTP requests to newapp.example.com now redirect to HTTPS with a 301.
